# Windows PRIMARY site — env NOTE (not a full template).
#
# There is NO separate Windows .env schema. The real .env is the SHARED one at
# deploy/mac-site/.env, generated by deploy/mac-site/secrets-pull.sh from the
# SAME Key Vault the mac-site uses. Do not duplicate the secret list here — see
# deploy/mac-site/.env.example for the authoritative template.
#
# The stack is brought up from deploy/mac-site (`docker compose --profile live up
# -d`), so it reads deploy/mac-site/.env. This file exists only to document the
# TWO Windows-specific overrides you must set in that shared .env.
#
# ── override #1: amd64 image tags (the ONLY arch difference from an arm64 host) ─
# x86-64 Windows runs the pipeline's NATIVE amd64 tags — the plain build number,
# NOT an `-arm64` side tag. Pin these to the registry build the cloud is running
# so the standby matches production. Example (bump the number in lockstep):
#   HONCHO_IMAGE_TAG=100
#   ROUTER_IMAGE_TAG=100
#   PAPERCLIP_IMAGE_TAG=100
#   MEMORY_GOVERNOR_IMAGE_TAG=100
# (On an arm64 host these would read 100-arm64. Everything else in .env is identical.)
#
# ── override #2: AAF_HOME points at the WSL user's home ─────────────────────
# The bash scripts default AAF_HOME to $HOME/aaf inside WSL; set it explicitly to
# the WSL user's home so logs, the lease mirror, and the local share copies land
# under the Linux filesystem (fast) rather than a /mnt/c path.
#   AAF_HOME=/home/<wsluser>/aaf
#
# Everything else (AZURE_PG_HOST, all [pull] secrets, the structural [fixed]
# overrides) is IDENTICAL to the mac-site and is written by secrets-pull.sh.
